//
// Expected: c1 — and the report has to show why.
//
// Ledger never sends or receives anything; all it does is leak the key that
// breaks the protocol. The diagram builder used to draw only principals that
// appear on some message, so Ledger and its `leaks` were absent from the
// sequence diagram in every format, and the report showed a protocol with no
// leak beside a broken confidentiality query. A principal that leaks now earns
// its lane whether or not it ever speaks.
attacker[passive]

principal Ledger[
	knows private k
	leaks k
]

principal Alice[
	knows private k
	knows private m
	e = ENC(k, m)
]

Alice -> Bob: e

principal Bob[
	knows private k
	d = DEC(k, e)
]

queries[
	confidentiality? m
]
